.TH FFMPEG-ENCODE 1 "July 2026" "ffmpeg-encode" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ffmpeg-encode \- VAAPI HEVC batch video encoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ffmpeg-encode
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B ffmpeg-encode
.B \-i
\fIDIR\fR
.B \-o
\fIDIR\fR
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B ffmpeg-encode
.B \-\-input
\fIFILE\fR
[\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ffmpeg-encode
is a thin wrapper around
.BR ffmpeg (1)
that encodes video with hardware-accelerated
.B hevc_vaapi
(VAAPI).
It can process a whole directory tree (batch mode) or a single file.
.P
By default it reads from
.I /mnt/shared/Compressing
and writes to
.IR /mnt/shared/Handbraked ,
preserving relative paths under the output directory.
.P
While encoding, a single coloured status line is shown (when stdout is a TTY):
.IP \(bu 2
percentage of the
.B current video
completed
.IP \(bu 2
percentage of the
.B queue
completed (weighted by finished files plus current progress)
.IP \(bu 2
encode
.B speed
in frames per second (fps)
.P
When the run finishes successfully, a size summary reports original size,
encoded size, and space saved (human-readable and as a percentage).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " DIR"
Input directory for batch mode. Default:
.IR /mnt/shared/Compressing .
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Output directory for batch mode. Default:
.IR /mnt/shared/Handbraked .
Relative paths under the input directory are preserved under this root.
.TP
.BI \-\-input " FILE"
Encode a single input file instead of scanning a directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
Output path for single-file mode. If omitted, the name is derived as
.IR basename-hevc.mkv
next to the input. The extension is always forced to
.BR .mkv
even if another extension is given.
.TP
.BI \-p " PRESET"
Speed / quality trade-off:
.RS
.TP
.B speed
Faster encode (\fB\-preset fast\fR).
.TP
.B balanced
Default. No extra preset flag.
.TP
.B quality
Slower, better quality (\fB\-preset slow\fR).
.RE
.TP
.BI \-q " QP"
Constant QP quality value for the VAAPI encoder. Default:
.BR 27 .
Lower values mean higher quality and larger files.
.TP
.BI \-j " N"
.BI \-\-jobs " N"
Encode up to
.I N
files in parallel (default:
.BR 1 ).
Useful for batches of many small files where per-process ffmpeg / VAAPI
startup would otherwise dominate; a value of 2 or 3 is a good fit for a
VCN-class GPU.
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run. Print the
.B ffmpeg
command that would be run; do not encode or delete anything.
.TP
.B \-D
Delete the original file after a successful encode.
This is
.B on by default
(the flag exists for explicit use; there is currently no opt-out flag).
.TP
.B \-h
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS Encoding
.IP \(bu 2
Video codec:
.B hevc_vaapi
via
.B \-hwaccel vaapi
.IP \(bu 2
Audio streams are
.B copied
(not re-encoded)
.IP \(bu 2
Only video and audio are mapped (\fB\-map 0:v? \-map 0:a?\fR); subtitles
are skipped to avoid failures on some broadcast sources (e.g. DVB/teletext on
.BR .ts )
.IP \(bu 2
Existing output files are overwritten (\fB\-y\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
All outputs use the
.B .mkv
(Matroska) container, regardless of the input extension
.SS Batch discovery
In batch mode, files are found recursively under the input directory with
extensions (case-insensitive):
.BR mkv ", " mp4 ", " avi ", " mov ", " webm ", " ts ", " mts ", " webp .
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.B ffmpeg
built with VAAPI support
.IP \(bu 2
.B vainfo
available (from
.BR libva-utils )
.IP \(bu 2
.B ffprobe
(for duration / progress)
.SH EXAMPLES
Encode everything under the default directories:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode
.EE
.P
Custom directories and quality preset:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-i ~/Videos/raw \-o ~/Videos/encoded \-p quality
.EE
.P
Single file, faster preset:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-\-input video.mkv \-\-output video\-hevc.mkv \-p speed
.EE
.P
Show the command without running it:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-n \-i ~/Videos/raw \-o ~/Videos/encoded
.EE
.P
Tighter quality (lower QP):
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-q 24
.EE
.P
Encode a batch of small files with three parallel jobs:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-i ~/Videos/raw \-o ~/Videos/encoded \-j 3
.EE
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.B p
Pause / resume encoding.
.TP
.B r
Resume encoding.
.TP
.B s
Skip the currently encoding file(s).
.TP
.B a
Add a file to the queue.
.TP
.B Up / Down, j / k
Scroll the queue list one line.
.TP
.B Page Up / Page Down
Scroll the queue list by half a page.
.TP
.B Home / End
Jump to the top / bottom of the queue.
.TP
.B f
Re-enable auto-follow, keeping the currently encoding file centred.
.P
Scrolling with the arrow keys turns off auto-follow so the queue stops
jumping around; note that a terminal only repaints the focused tab, so an
unfocused tab may appear frozen until you switch back to it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All encodes succeeded (or dry run completed).
.TP
.B 1
One or more encodes failed, invalid options, missing input, or VAAPI
unavailable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /mnt/shared/Compressing
Default input directory (batch mode).
.TP
.I /mnt/shared/Handbraked
Default output directory (batch mode).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR vainfo (1)
.SH BUGS
Deleting the original after a successful encode is enabled by default and
cannot currently be turned off with a flag (only via editing the script
defaults).
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use with VAAPI on AMD RDNA4 (RX 9070 class).
